  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "The cult leader Charles Manson is said to have modelled his life on Stranger in a Strange Land, a novel by the science fiction writer Robert Heinlein, and to have carried the book around with him in the 1960s. Michels says this himself, without naming a source, in a conversation that also takes in Jolly West, a figure he ties to the CIA's mind control research. If true, it would mean a piece of fiction helped shape one of the most notorious groups of the era."
